{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages","id":1031499,"title":"Putting on the Pressure on Mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-14T01:57:08-08:00","id":1031499,"title":"Putting on the Pressure on Mages","content":"Midway through the second season of our Mage: Manila campaign, and looking for ways to raise the stakes, increase the pressure, and basically tempt my players to spend more and more Reach to deal with crises Most of them are Gnosis 3, with 3 dots in a Ruling Arcanum.<br /> <br /> I know this has been asked before, but what are some of the ways you've raised the ante in your game? Would love to hear your stories!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T03:42:59-08:00","id":1031521,"title":"","content":"The easiest way is to simply introduce challenges in the scene in waves. This works especially well if they haven't bothered to look very far ahead or do a lot of investigation into whatever trouble they're about to get into.<br /> <br /> So, for example in my game, the players were meeting up with some Sleeper friends at a lecture. One of the attendees was attacked by a bug-like thing that wasn't a goetia but was only visible on the Mind Attuned Twilight spectrum. They managed to pin it with a Telekinesis spell pretty handily, made the spell last all day and kept going figuring once they got their Sleeper friends out of the way they could come back and investigate it at their leisure. On their way out the door someone got jumped by another bug. They pinned that one too, but since they're both Gnosis 1 now they're Reaching. Well, the Obrimos was, the Mastigos was preoccupied with keeping the Sleepers moving. Then another bug appears and jumps a target in the parking lot. I could have easily kept going (In fact as they were escaping they could feel their PMS trigger two more times meaning that there were probably more bugs who had succeeded in attacking innocent bystanders), but I didn't and luckily for them they managed to get away without scoring a Paradox. There was definitely a lot of Reach being spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T08:19:13-08:00","id":1031591,"title":"","content":"Truth be told, you rarely have to worry about raising the ante; normal investigation will do it. The fewer dots Mages have, the more tempted they'll be to use those advantages to their maximum effect and, thus, the more likely they are to invoke Paradox.<br /> <br /> You <i>never</i> have enough Reach to do what you want. Mages will find a few select rotes to do the things they like to do or find necessary to do a lot, but that aside, they're always going to risk Paradox <i>some</i> time or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:28:35-08:00","id":1031664,"title":"","content":"Well it might be the most useless of answers, but throw a tough mystery at them; a mystery that's been so obscured that it's going to take more than they've got to get to the bottom of it. Also, as the mystery goes along don't forget that mages have to pay attention to stuff other than their mysteries; there are so many things that can distract them in the world of darkness, and sometimes you might want to send these distractions at them to open up new avenues of investigation, or have the characters make tough decisions that will affect them later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T11:06:00-08:00","id":1031689,"title":"","content":"One way is to have their works tampering with the works of other Mages for unrelated reasons. Anything in the world around them can be of the interest of another Mage, and so be enhanced, watched, weakened or warded in any way, for completely unrelated reasons. Or maybe for tangentially related reasons. Just think about your characters being unintended targets for a very good Fate effect...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T12:13:03-08:00","id":1031727,"title":"","content":"I'd also say that the game isn't about making Mages cause Paradoxes and that isn't the only or even the best way to put pressure on Mages. Have their objective inside the territory of another Mage for instance and this introduces a slew of complications depending on how they navigate that particular problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:52:01-08:00","id":1036854,"title":"","content":"I ran my first full session on Saturday and it was Reach city. Just trying to get Sensory &amp; Instant for 3-dot spells is creating Reach issues. By the end of the scene two Mages had base Paradox pools of 3 dice and the other one was at 4. I could see Mana being very useful in a long fight...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:07:00-08:00","id":1036859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages#post1031499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Midway through the second season of our Mage: Manila campaign, and looking for ways to raise the stakes, increase the pressure, and basically tempt my players to spend more and more Reach to deal with crises Most of them are Gnosis 3, with 3 dots in a Ruling Arcanum.<br /> <br /> I know this has been asked before, but what are some of the ways you've raised the ante in your game? Would love to hear your stories!</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget that they're mortal, and have mortal lives. Mages that are just Mages are the exception, not the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6783-notanautomaton","name":"notanautomaton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:54:25-08:00","id":1038212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1031521#post1031521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest way is to simply introduce challenges in the scene in waves. This works especially well if they haven't bothered to look very far ahead or do a lot of investigation into whatever trouble they're about to get into.<br /> <br /> So, for example in my game, the players were meeting up with some Sleeper friends at a lecture. One of the attendees was attacked by a bug-like thing that wasn't a goetia but was only visible on the Mind Attuned Twilight spectrum. They managed to pin it with a Telekinesis spell pretty handily, made the spell last all day and kept going figuring once they got their Sleeper friends out of the way they could come back and investigate it at their leisure. On their way out the door someone got jumped by another bug. They pinned that one too, but since they're both Gnosis 1 now they're Reaching. Well, the Obrimos was, the Mastigos was preoccupied with keeping the Sleepers moving. Then another bug appears and jumps a target in the parking lot. I could have easily kept going (In fact as they were escaping they could feel their PMS trigger two more times meaning that there were probably more bugs who had succeeded in attacking innocent bystanders), but I didn't and luckily for them they managed to get away without scoring a Paradox. There was definitely a lot of Reach being spent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for sharing the anecdote. Adding the pressure in waves <i>does</i> a sense of increasing tension, and impending disaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:57:54-08:00","id":1038214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1031591#post1031591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truth be told, you rarely have to worry about raising the ante; normal investigation will do it. The fewer dots Mages have, the more tempted they'll be to use those advantages to their maximum effect and, thus, the more likely they are to invoke Paradox.<br /> <br /> You <i>never</i> have enough Reach to do what you want. Mages will find a few select rotes to do the things they like to do or find necessary to do a lot, but that aside, they're always going to risk Paradox <i>some</i> time or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do have a point. So far, my players have been finding ways to really exceed their Reach in hopes of doing overly ambitious things. It seems to just come naturally. I just worry sometimes that I make it too easy for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:00:31-08:00","id":1038216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1031664#post1031664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it might be the most useless of answers, but throw a tough mystery at them; a mystery that's been so obscured that it's going to take more than they've got to get to the bottom of it. Also, as the mystery goes along don't forget that mages have to pay attention to stuff other than their mysteries; there are so many things that can distract them in the world of darkness, and sometimes you might want to send these distractions at them to open up new avenues of investigation, or have the characters make tough decisions that will affect them later on.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right on. Mages are still human after all, and life happens. One of the things I'm exploring next is to have their 'normal' lives interfere with chasing Mysteries. Thank you for chiming in!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:04:09-08:00","id":1038221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1031727#post1031727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also say that the game isn't about making Mages cause Paradoxes and that isn't the only or even the best way to put pressure on Mages. Have their objective inside the territory of another Mage for instance and this introduces a slew of complications depending on how they navigate that particular problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what you're saying, I get that trying too hard to set up Paradoxes isn't the way to go. Good point. Right now, the players have intruded on the territory of another mage (supposedly dead for decades, but not really). Thanks for sharing your thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:08:10-08:00","id":1038225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1036854#post1036854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran my first full session on Saturday and it was Reach city. Just trying to get Sensory &amp; Instant for 3-dot spells is creating Reach issues. By the end of the scene two Mages had base Paradox pools of 3 dice and the other one was at 4. I could see Mana being very useful in a long fight...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana is precious indeed. Apart from the Obrimos player, everyone else is carefully conserving theirs. What happened to your mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:30:43-08:00","id":1038248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1038214#post1038214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do have a point. So far, my players have been finding ways to really exceed their Reach in hopes of doing overly ambitious things. It seems to just come naturally. I just worry sometimes that I make it too easy for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worry about making it fun first. Are they having fun? If yes, then you're doing it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T23:35:09-08:00","id":1038285,"title":"","content":"As to Mysteries - to make them harder but also more rewarding - think about making them 'locked' with other Mysteries. If your chronicle is about Mystery A, but you lock it to Mystery B and C, it will make game more varied, but also a bit more harder and not just forcing things straight to Mystery A. Locking Mysteries are described in document linked to <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/i-can-see-for-miles-and-miles-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">this Open Dev post</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T09:04:19-08:00","id":1038441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages#post1031499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Midway through the second season of our Mage: Manila campaign, and looking for ways to raise the stakes, increase the pressure, and basically tempt my players to spend more and more Reach to deal with crises Most of them are Gnosis 3, with 3 dots in a Ruling Arcanum.<br /> <br /> I know this has been asked before, but what are some of the ways you've raised the ante in your game? Would love to hear your stories!</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't really Mage or even CoD but in one game where I had a powerful sorcerer I introduced the concept of a pariah (originally from an unknown science fantasy setting near you...) which is a person who is immune to magic. It just don't stick on them, can't be scryied, no empathic links, can't be targeted...and then sent a few of those after the magician. We didn't get to the final showdown but I got a feeling the player was sweating all the way we got.<br /> <br /> Or failing that, let some form of artefact, potentially connected with the Supernal Realms, be found in the city and see all hell raised over all the people who wants to get hold of it.Could have powerful Mages from outside of the city coming in to shake things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T09:22:14-08:00","id":1038448,"title":"","content":"Set one of the Bound free upon the PCs or the area?<br /> Or, Supernal Entities are hunting them for unknown reasons.<br /> Or, some Abyssal being is attacking them through the Astral and/or their Sympathetic Connections. Leave your friends/family open to attack, or distance yourself from them?<br /> Or, Banishers. Banishers everywhere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:03:55-08:00","id":1040426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1038225#post1038225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mana is precious indeed. Apart from the Obrimos player, everyone else is carefully conserving theirs. What happened to your mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only the first session, but a gang decided to have a party in the woods right near their sanctum. They would have ignored it, but the bonfire they made was potentially going to burn the forest down.<br /> <br /> The Obrimos turned invisible and moved to where the gang was so that he could make it rain on their party and make them want to leave. A lot of scale factors for that spell.<br /> <br /> The Mastigos was casting instant, sensory and remote spells through the camera system to help the Obrimos.<br /> <br /> The Thyrsus sent a couple deer into the area to spook the gang, but a drugged up gang member ended up chasing the deer. They isolated him and found out that he was carrying an Acamoth for some reason.<br /> <br /> They ended up in a fight with this enhanced gang member and the Thyrsus was forced to use Knit at sensory range a few times.<br /> <br /> It was a good session and each Mage spent about 3 Mana during the encounter.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm finding is that it's not always possible to use your dedicated tool as a Yantra, because it doesn't always have semiotic significance. This makes Paradox more of a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T22:31:07-08:00","id":1040436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1040426#post1040426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm finding is that it's not always possible to use your dedicated tool as a Yantra, because it doesn't always have semiotic significance. This makes Paradox more of a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can explicitly use it even when it doesn't have semiotic significance for the Paradox Reduction","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T23:08:19-08:00","id":1040453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1038441#post1038441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't really Mage or even CoD but in one game where I had a powerful sorcerer I introduced the concept of a pariah (originally from an unknown science fantasy setting near you...) which is a person who is immune to magic. It just don't stick on them, can't be scryied, no empathic links, can't be targeted...and then sent a few of those after the magician. We didn't get to the final showdown but I got a feeling the player was sweating all the way we got.<br /> <br /> Or failing that, let some form of artefact, potentially connected with the Supernal Realms, be found in the city and see all hell raised over all the people who wants to get hold of it.Could have powerful Mages from outside of the city coming in to shake things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing with this kind of thing is that in any system even a quarter as flexible as Mage magic immune stuff like this (unless supernaturally powerful in other ways) has to be able to disable magic in a large area around themselves. Otherwise it's a simple matter of just killing/disabling them indirectly. Throw a rock at them at the speed of a bullet, drop large structures on them, shape the ground under them and trap them in a deep hole, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T23:50:08-08:00","id":1040460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1040453#post1040453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with this kind of thing is that in any system even a quarter as flexible as Mage magic immune stuff like this (unless supernaturally powerful in other ways) has to be able to disable magic in a large area around themselves. Otherwise it's a simple matter of just killing/disabling them indirectly. Throw a rock at them at the speed of a bullet, drop large structures on them, shape the ground under them and trap them in a deep hole, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. In that setting magic wasn't as multisided as in MtA so you would probably need to include a &quot;nill zone&quot; for magic around these guys at the least in MtA. But I do think that its an interesting thing to essentially put some kind of anti-magic enemy against the Mages and see if they can make a hole through that anti-magic wall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:33:39-08:00","id":1040533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031499-putting-on-the-pressure-on-mages?p=1040460#post1040460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very true. In that setting magic wasn't as multisided as in MtA so you would probably need to include a &quot;nill zone&quot; for magic around these guys at the least in MtA. But I do think that its an interesting thing to essentially put some kind of anti-magic enemy against the Mages and see if they can make a hole through that anti-magic wall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of the Ansho from the Tokyo setting for Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}